.TH playmod 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
playmod \- play a MOD tracker file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playmod
.I file.mod
[\fIvolume\fR [\fBnoloop\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B playmod
plays an Amiga-style MOD file.  Unlike the sampled formats it is
synthesised from a handful of short samples and a pattern list, so it is
small on the card and cheap to play.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I volume
0 to 100.
.TP
.B noloop
Play once and stop.  Without it the tune repeats, which is what a MOD
usually expects.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# playmod tune.mod 70
# playmod tune.mod 70 noloop
# playmod tune.mod 50 &
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR playmp3 (1),
.BR kill (1)
